**Top 10 Beginner Mistakes:**

**1. Class Name != Filename**
```java
// ❌ File: Demo.java
public class HelloWorld { }
// Error: class HelloWorld is public, should be declared in a file named HelloWorld.java

// ✅ File: HelloWorld.java
public class HelloWorld { }
```

**2. Wrong Main Method Signature**
```java
// ❌ Wrong
public void main(String[] args) { } // Not static
public static void Main(String[] args) { } // Wrong case
public static void main(String args[]) { } // Wrong parameter type

// ✅ Correct
public static void main(String[] args) { }
```

**3. Missing Semicolon**
```java
// ❌ Wrong
System.out.println("Hello")
// Error: ';' expected

// ✅ Correct
System.out.println("Hello");
```

**4. Mismatched Braces**
```java
// ❌ Wrong
public class Test {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Hello");
    } // Missing closing brace for class
// Error: reached end of file while parsing

// ✅ Correct  
public class Test {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Hello");
    }
}
```

**5. Case Sensitivity**
```java
// ❌ Wrong
System.Out.Println("Hello"); // Wrong case
string name = "John"; // string not String

// ✅ Correct
System.out.println("Hello");
String name = "John";
```

**6. Running .java Instead of .class**
```bash
# ❌ Wrong
$ java HelloWorld.java
# Error: Could not find or load main class HelloWorld.java

# ✅ Correct
$ javac HelloWorld.java
$ java HelloWorld
```

**7. Package Mismatch**
```java
// ❌ File in com/example/ folder
public class Test { } // No package declaration

// ✅ Correct
package com.example;
public class Test { }
```

**8. Missing Parentheses**
```java
// ❌ Wrong
System.out.println "Hello"; // Missing ()

// ✅ Correct
System.out.println("Hello");
```

**9. Typos in Keywords**
```java
// ❌ Wrong
Public class Test { } // Capital P
static publc void main { } // publc instead of public

// ✅ Correct
public class Test { }
public static void main(String[] args) { }
```

**10. Forgetting to Import**
```java
// ❌ Wrong (if Scanner not imported)
Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
// Error: cannot find symbol

// ✅ Correct
import java.util.Scanner;
Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
```

**Debugging Tips:**
- Read error messages carefully
- Check line numbers in errors
- Use IDE syntax highlighting
- Compile frequently

