**Java Naming Conventions:**

**1. Classes & Interfaces - PascalCase**
```java
// ✅ Correct
public class StudentManager { }
public class HelloWorld { }
public interface Drawable { }

// ❌ Wrong
public class studentmanager { }  // lowercase
public class student_manager { } // underscore
public class STUDENTMANAGER { }  // all caps
```

**2. Methods & Variables - camelCase**
```java
// ✅ Correct
public void calculateTotal() { }
int studentAge = 20;
String firstName = "John";

// ❌ Wrong
public void CalculateTotal() { }  // PascalCase
int StudentAge = 20;  // PascalCase
String first_name = "John";  // snake_case
```

**3. Constants - UPPER_SNAKE_CASE**
```java
// ✅ Correct
public static final int MAX_SIZE = 100;
public static final String DATABASE_URL = "jdbc:mysql://localhost";
public static final double PI_VALUE = 3.14159;

// ❌ Wrong
public static final int maxSize = 100;  // camelCase
public static final int Max_Size = 100;  // Mixed case
```

**4. Packages - lowercase.with.dots**
```java
// ✅ Correct
package com.company.project;
package org.example.util;

// ❌ Wrong
package Com.Company.Project;  // Mixed case
package com_company_project;  // Underscores
```

**5. Enum Types - PascalCase (same as classes)**
```java
// ✅ Correct
public enum DayOfWeek {
    MONDAY, TUESDAY, WEDNESDAY  // Constants in all caps
}

public enum Status {
    ACTIVE, INACTIVE, PENDING
}
```

**Summary Table:**
| Type | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|----------|
| Class | PascalCase | `StudentManager` |
| Interface | PascalCase | `Drawable` |
| Method | camelCase | `calculateTotal()` |
| Variable | camelCase | `firstName` |
| Constant | UPPER_SNAKE_CASE | `MAX_SIZE` |
| Package | lowercase | `com.example` |
| Enum Type | PascalCase | `DayOfWeek` |
| Enum Constant | UPPER_CASE | `MONDAY` |

**Additional Rules:**
- Use meaningful, descriptive names
- Avoid single-letter names (except i, j, k for loops)
- Avoid abbreviations unless widely known
- Boolean variables: start with is/has/can
  ```java
  boolean isActive = true;
  boolean hasPermission = false;
  boolean canEdit = true;
  ```

